WEBVTT

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:15.000
<v Hana>Thanks everyone. We have two items today: the senior backend role and the junior designer role.</v>

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:27.000
<v Hana>Let's start with backend. We have two finalists, Noor and Oleg.</v>

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:42.000
<v Marcus>I interviewed both. Noor was excellent on system design. She walked through a sync conflict problem better than most of us would.</v>

00:00:52.000 --> 00:01:01.000
<v Priya>How was her communication? That matters for this team.</v>

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:16.000
<v Marcus>Clear and calm. The only concern is her notice period, which is three months.</v>

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:33.000
<v Gus>Three months is long but acceptable for a senior hire. What about Oleg?</v>

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:48.000
<v Marcus>Oleg is technically solid, but his system design answers stayed very generic.</v>

00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:09.000
<v Priya>I did the culture interview with Oleg. He interrupted a lot and dismissed two of my questions as unimportant. I would not want him on this team.</v>

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:33.000
<v Gus>That is serious. Hana, did anyone else flag it?</v>

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:47.000
<v Hana>Yes, the panel feedback mentions it twice.</v>

00:02:48.000 --> 00:03:01.000
<v Gus>Then my decision is that we do not move forward with Oleg.</v>

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:07.000
<v Priya>Agreed.</v>

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:14.000
<v Marcus>Agreed.</v>

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:29.000
<v Gus>And we extend an offer to Noor, at band five.</v>

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:44.000
<v Hana>Before I send anything, I need the extra backend headcount approved. It has not been approved yet.</v>

00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:07.000
<v Gus>That is on me. I'll get the headcount approval to you by Monday.</v>

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:22.000
<v Hana>Once I have it, I'll send Noor the offer letter by Wednesday.</v>

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:35.000
<v Marcus>Should Noor meet the team before accepting?</v>

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:50.000
<v Priya>Good idea, but only if she asks. We don't want to delay the offer.</v>

00:04:52.000 --> 00:05:06.000
<v Gus>Fine, optional then.</v>

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:24.000
<v Marcus>I'll write the feedback summary for Oleg's rejection, so Hana can send him something respectful.</v>

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:35.000
<v Hana>Thanks, Marcus. When can I have it?</v>

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:49.000
<v Marcus>By tomorrow end of day.</v>

00:05:50.000 --> 00:06:04.000
<v Hana>Now the junior designer role. We only have four applicants and none look strong.</v>

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:24.000
<v Priya>Honestly, with the roadmap shifting I don't need a junior designer before the new year.</v>

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:43.000
<v Gus>Then let's pause the junior designer hiring until January.</v>

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:58.000
<v Hana>Pause until January, understood. I'll let the four applicants know.</v>

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:19.000
<v Hana>One more idea. Our referral bonus is low compared to other companies. I would suggest raising it from one thousand to two thousand euros.</v>

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:44.000
<v Gus>Maybe, but that needs finance to look at it. I wouldn't decide it today.</v>

00:07:48.000 --> 00:08:01.000
<v Priya>Agreed, let's not decide it today.</v>

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:16.000
<v Marcus>Related question: what is our relocation budget for senior hires? Noor is already local, but we may need it for future roles.</v>

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:39.000
<v Hana>I don't know. Nobody has defined a relocation budget yet.</v>

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:51.000
<v Gus>Then that is open.</v>

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:59.000
<v Hana>Great, I think that's everything. Thank you.</v>
